{
  "name": "ClinicIQ — Newsletter Engine",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ClinicIQ — Newsletter Engine (2026-08-21)\n\n**Subscribe.** The site's footer form → Netlify function `newsletter` → this workflow (webhook path `cliniciqsubs`, taken over from the legacy workflow — same path, same webhookId). Inserts the email into the `cliniciq_emails` data table as a row with `message = 'newsletter signup'` (deduped by email) and sends a branded welcome email with a working unsubscribe link.\n\n**Unsubscribe.** Every email carries a per-recipient link:\n`https://johnsaenz.au/webhook/cliniciqunsub?id=<rowId>&email=<email>`\nThe GET webhook deletes the matching row (both id AND email must match) and returns a confirmation HTML page. Only rows still in the table receive broadcasts — so unsubscribed means gone from the list.\n\n⚠️ **Audience scoping:** `cliniciq_emails` also holds historical contact-form messages (the legacy contact webhook wrote there). Every subscriber query filters on `message = 'newsletter signup'` so contact-form rows are NEVER emailed. Do not remove that filter.\n\n⚠️ **Audience scoping:** `cliniciq_emails` also holds historical contact-form messages (the legacy contact webhook wrote there). Every subscriber query filters on `message = 'newsletter signup'` so contact-form rows are NEVER emailed. Do not remove that filter.\n\n**Broadcast (Telegram → AI → email).** A 1-minute schedule polls the Telegram bot API directly over HTTP (no n8n credential needed):\n1. Create a bot with @BotFather → copy the token.\n2. Paste the token into the `telegram settings` Code node (replace `PASTE_BOT_TOKEN_HERE`) — or set workflow static data `{\"telegram\":{\"botToken\":\"...\"}}`.\n3. Send `/start` to your bot — the first account to /start becomes the admin (stored in static data). Only the admin's messages trigger broadcasts.\n4. Text the bot your newsletter notes → AI (gpt-4.1-mini) builds a branded HTML email (subject + body, `{{UNSUB_URL}}` placeholder in the footer) → sent to every subscriber with a personal unsubscribe link → the bot replies with the send count.\n\nA poll lock (90s TTL in static data) prevents overlapping runs double-sending; the getUpdates offset is committed before processing for the same reason.\n\n**Test hook.** POST `cliniciqbroadcasttest` with `{\"secret\":\"TEST_SECRET_PLACEHOLDER\",\"text\":\"...\"}` runs the same AI→send chain without Telegram (used for E2E testing).\n\n⚠️ The 24-month retention cleanup also purges `cliniciq_emails` rows, so subscriptions older than 24 months lapse (conservative consent refresh, consistent with Privacy Policy s9).",
        "height": 1232,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 4
      },
