    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Telegram bot config lives in workflow static data so no n8n credential\n// is needed. Set the token once (edit the DEFAULT below, or set static data\n// {\"telegram\":{\"botToken\":\"...\"}}). The first /start to the bot becomes\n// the admin. A 90s poll lock stops overlapping runs double-sending.\nconst DEFAULT_TOKEN = 'PASTE_BOT_TOKEN_HERE';\nconst sd = $getWorkflowStaticData('global');\nsd.telegram = sd.telegram || {};\nconst token = sd.telegram.botToken || DEFAULT_TOKEN;\nconst adminChatId = String(sd.telegram.adminChatId || '');\nconst offset = Number(sd.telegram.lastUpdateId || 0);\nconst lock = Number(sd.telegram.lock || 0);\nconst configured = token !== DEFAULT_TOKEN && token.length > 10;\nconst locked = Date.now() - lock < 90000;\nif (configured && !locked) sd.telegram.lock = Date.now();\nreturn [{ json: { configured, locked, token, adminChatId, offset } }];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        192,
        96
      ],
      "id": "c1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000019",
      "name": "telegram settings"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "c1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000020",
              "leftValue": "={{ Boolean($json.configured && !$json.locked) }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        400,
        96
      ],
      "id": "c1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000021",
      "name": "bot configured?"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "={{ 'https://api.telegram.org/bot' + $('telegram settings').first().json.token + '/getUpdates?timeout=1&offset=' + ($('telegram settings').first().json.offset + 1) }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 15000
        }
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        608,
        96
      ],
      "id": "c1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000022",
      "name": "get updates",
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Commit the getUpdates offset BEFORE processing so overlapping polls never\n// re-send. Only the admin's non-command text messages become broadcasts.\nconst sd = $getWorkflowStaticData('global');\nsd.telegram = sd.telegram || {};\nconst body = items[0].json || {};\nconst updates = Array.isArray(body.result) ? body.result : [];\nif (!updates.length) { sd.telegram.lock = 0; return []; }\nsd.telegram.lastUpdateId = Math.max(...updates.map((u) => u.update_id));\n\nlet admin = String(sd.telegram.adminChatId || '');\nconst out = [];\nfor (const u of updates) {\n  const msg = u.message || u.channel_post;\n  if (!msg || !msg.chat) continue;\n  const chatId = String(msg.chat.id);\n  const text = String(msg.text || '').trim();\n  if (!admin && text === '/start') {\n    // First account to /start the bot becomes the admin (solo operator).\n    admin = chatId;\n    sd.telegram.adminChatId = chatId;\n    continue;\n  }\n  if (!admin || chatId !== admin) continue;\n  if (!text || text.startsWith('/')) continue;\n  out.push({ json: { text, chatId } });\n}\nif (!out.length) sd.telegram.lock = 0;\nreturn out;"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        816,
        96
      ],
      "id": "c1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000023",
      "name": "handle updates"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "={{ $json.text }}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=# ROLE\nYou are the newsletter builder for ClinicIQ Solutions (cliniciq.com.au) — AI tools, calculators and overlays for Australian practice nurses in GP clinics. The founder, John Saenz (Registered Nurse), sends you rough notes; you turn them into one polished HTML email.\n\n# FACTS you may rely on (use only if relevant — never invent pricing)\n- Free tier on every tool; Pro is $29–$39/month per tool (NursePod $39; Docsert AI / cIQventory / PIPQI $29), month-to-month, no practice sign-off needed.\n- NursePod — shift task list: smart prioritisation, task dashboards, handover communication hub.\n- Docsert AI — sorts and structures documents in minutes; user review and customisation always required. It is a document tool, not a medical device.\n- cIQventory — treatment-room stock: supply prediction, vaccine/consumable expiry tracking, reorder alerts.\n- PIPQI — all PIP QI measures in one dashboard with national benchmarks.\n- Plus free clinical & business calculators, RACGP-aligned templates and downloads.\n\n# EMAIL STYLE\n- Australian English, warm and practical, speaking to an individual practice nurse (\"you\", \"your shift\").\n- Subject: short, specific, no clickbait, under 60 characters.\n- One HTML email: single column, max-width 600px, table-based, INLINE STYLES ONLY (no <style> blocks), email-client safe.\n- Brand: header band background #2C4A3C containing the logo (https://downloads.cliniciq.com.au/icons/cliniciq-logo.png, width 140); body on #ffffff; accent colour #C4A661; text #111827; system font stack; generous padding.\n- Structure: header → short greeting → 1–3 short sections from John's notes (<h2> about 18px, <p> 15px line-height 1.6) → one call-to-action button (background #2C4A3C, white text, linking to https://cliniciq.com.au) → footer.\n- Footer (mandatory, exactly this shape): 12px #6b7280 text: \"You're receiving this because you subscribed at cliniciq.com.au\" · <a href=\"{{UNSUB_URL}}\">Unsubscribe</a> · \"ClinicIQ Solutions — cliniciq.com.au\".\n- Keep John's meaning, tighten the wording. Never invent offers, prices, dates, features or statistics. Never give clinical or medical advice. Keep body copy under ~300 words.\n\n# OUTPUT (MANDATORY)\nReply with ONLY this JSON object — no code fences, no commentary:\n{\"subject\": \"<subject line>\", \"html\": \"<full HTML document>\"}\nThe html must contain the literal placeholder {{UNSUB_URL}} exactly once, in the footer unsubscribe link.\n"
        }
      },
